{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Come to Pharaoh, for I have hardened his heart and the heart of his servants.</b> In all the plagues we do not find this expression, only now. But since Pharaoh said, 'HaShem is righteous, and I and my people are the wicked,' and afterward it writes, 'he continued to sin, he and his servants,' it was necessary to say thus: <b>for I have hardened</b> etc. — that is, do not wonder that they continued to sin after he said 'HaShem is righteous,' for I have hardened his heart and the heart of his servants."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:47.761580807Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}